# =====================================================================
# Release V046 -- practitioner diary `day` field (working hours were blank)
# =====================================================================
# Real Dentally rota_practitioner_diaries carries the date in `day`; the mock used `date`.
# Bronze read only `date`, so for real tenants Day came through NULL -> Silver.Practitioner_Diary.Day
# NULL -> Fact_Practitioner_Diaries.Day_Date / fk_Date_Day NULL -> the daily aggregate couldn't
# attribute Available_Clinical_Mins to a day -> Worked_Hours NULL -> Chair Utilisation,
# Revenue Per Clinical Hour, and Days-Until-Next-Free all blank.
#
# Fix (SP-only): Bronze reads COALESCE([day],[date]) -- real uses `day`, mock uses `date`; stage
# carries both columns (mergeSchema) so no view/validation change. Available_Clinical_Mins was
# already computed correctly; only the day attribution was missing.
#
# AFTER deploy: re-run Orchestrate_Build (build-only, T100). No truncate needed -- the diary chain
# updates via the hash gate (Day NULL->date changes the hash), and the daily aggregate +
# Fact_Metric_Actuals full-rebuild each run, so Worked_Hours repopulates and the working-hours
# cards light up. TODO (generator realism): generate_data.py should emit `day` not `date` for
# diary entries so synthetic tenants match (COALESCE covers it meanwhile).
#
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V046__diary_day_field.manifest -SkipTests
# =====================================================================

DEPLOY   Fabric\Bronze.usp_Load_Practitioner_Diary_Entries.StoredProcedure.sql

TEST
